{title: 416 - The Judgment Has Set}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #416 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Db}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 416}
{meta: category Doctrines - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Db]The judgment has set, the books have [C/G]been [Db/Ab]opened;
[Db/Ab]How shall we [Ab]stand in that [Gb]great [Fm]day,
[Ab7]When every [Db]thought, and word, and action,
[Db/Ab]God, the righteous [C/G]Judge, [Db/Ab]shall [Ebm/Bb]weigh?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Db/Ab]How shall [Ab]we stand in [Db/Ab]that [Ab7]great [Db/Ab]day?
[Ebm/Gb]How shall [Db/F]we stand in that great day?
[Bbm]Shall we be [Cdim]found [Gb/Db]before [Db/Ab]Him wanting?
[Bbm]Or with our sins all [Cdim]washed away?
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Db]The work is begun with those who [C/G]are [Db/Ab]sleeping,
[Db/Ab]Soon will the [Ab]living here [Gb]be [Fm]tried,
[Ab7]Out of [Db/Ab]the books of God's remembrance,
[Db/Ab]His decision [C/G]to [Db/Ab]abide.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Db]O, how shall we stand that moment [C/G]of [Db/Ab]searching,
[Db/Ab]When all our [Ab]sins those books [Gb]reveal?
[Ab7]When from [Db/Ab]that court, each case decided,
[Db/Ab]Shall be granted [C/G]no [Db/Ab]appeal?
{end_of_verse}
